IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `fcr-dates`

-- Federal Court Rules 2011 (Cth) -- the rules a person bringing or answering a claim in the Federal Court of Australia
-- meets: time, starting the claim and serving it, the defence and default, medical examinations, offers to settle,
-- discontinuance, damages calculated by a Registrar, appeals, judgments and interest, and costs.
--
-- Based on content from the Federal Register of Legislation: "Federal Court Rules 2011", Compilation No. 11
-- (compilation date 11 June 2026, register id F2026C00512), Commonwealth of Australia, licensed under CC BY 4.0
-- (https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/). Quotations are from the deposited plain-text conversion at
-- ../../registers/source-bundle/F2011L01551.txt. BASELINE ENCODING. Not for public use as advice. See NOTES.md.
--
-- Negatives follow the rulings of 2026-11-04 and 2026-11-05 (docs/ENCODING-GUIDE.md section 5): JUST FALSE where the
-- text itself says no; NOTHING where it does not answer, each tagged "NOTHING-kind" with the reason. Where the Court
-- decides (it "may", it "gives leave", it is "satisfied"), JUST TRUE means the Court can do it, never that it will; the
-- Court's judgments are inputs. Rule 1.35 (the Court may make an order inconsistent with these Rules) and rule 1.39
-- (the Court may extend or shorten any time) stand behind every answer and are not computed.

§ `Federal Court Rules 2011`

GIVEN b IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`yes or no` b MEANS
    IF b
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE

§§ `Part 2 -- filing (r 2.25(3))`

-- r 2.25(3): a document emailed or faxed to a Registry and accepted is "taken to have been filed: (a) if the whole
-- document is received by 4.30 pm on a business day for the Registry--on that day; or (b) in any other case--on the
-- next business day". Filing is therefore done only on business days, which brings in r 1.61(4) (fork F3).
GIVEN `the day it was received` IS A DATE, `received whole by 4.30 pm` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A DATE
`r 2.25(3) -- the day it is taken to be filed` `the day it was received` `received whole by 4.30 pm` MEANS
    IF `is a business day` `the day it was received` AND `received whole by 4.30 pm`
    THEN `the day it was received`
    ELSE `the next business day after` `the day it was received`

-- The last day to file a document within n days after a day: r 1.61(2), (3), (5), and (4) because filing is done only
-- on business days. ("file" means "file and serve": Dictionary.)
GIVEN x IS A DATE, n IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DATE
`the last day to file` x n MEANS `r 1.61 -- the last day of n days after` x n TRUE

-- The last day to do an act that is not filing (serving, paying, giving notice) within n days after a day.
GIVEN x IS A DATE, n IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DATE
`the last day to act` x n MEANS `r 1.61 -- the last day of n days after` x n FALSE

§§ `Part 8 -- starting the claim (rr 8.02, 8.03, 8.05, 8.06)`

-- r 8.02(1): "If Part 2 of the Civil Dispute Resolution Act applies to a proceeding, the applicant must, when filing the
-- applicant's originating application, file the applicant's genuine steps statement". Whether Part 2 applies is a
-- borrowed question (Civil Dispute Resolution Act 2011, not deposited here). The "if" unmet: JUST FALSE for this rule
-- (case by case, fork F4).
GIVEN `Part 2 of the Civil Dispute Resolution Act applies` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`r 8.02 -- I must file a genuine steps statement` `Part 2 of the Civil Dispute Resolution Act applies` MEANS
    `yes or no` `Part 2 of the Civil Dispute Resolution Act applies`

DECLARE `Practice note position` IS ONE OF
    `no practice note provides for an alternative document`
    `a practice note requires an alternative accompanying document`
    `a practice note permits an alternative accompanying document`

DECLARE `Accompanying document` IS ONE OF
    `a statement of claim`
    `a statement of claim or an affidavit`
    `the alternative accompanying document`
    `the alternative accompanying document or a statement of claim`
    `the alternative accompanying document, a statement of claim or an affidavit`

-- r 8.05(1) (relief includes damages) and (2) (relief does not include damages), paragraphs (a)-(c).
GIVEN `I claim damages` IS A BOOLEAN, `the practice note position` IS A `Practice note position`
GIVETH AN `Accompanying document`
`r 8.05 -- what must accompany the originating application` `I claim damages` `the practice note position` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the practice note position`
    WHEN `a practice note requires an alternative accompanying document` THEN `the alternative accompanying document`
    WHEN `a practice note permits an alternative accompanying document` THEN
        IF `I claim damages`
        THEN `the alternative accompanying document or a statement of claim`
        ELSE `the alternative accompanying document, a statement of claim or an affidavit`
    WHEN `no practice note provides for an alternative document` THEN
        IF `I claim damages`
        THEN `a statement of claim`
        ELSE `a statement of claim or an affidavit`

-- r 8.03(2) item 4: an originating application claiming exemplary damages must state "The claim for exemplary damages".
-- (r 8.03(3): it "need not include a claim for costs".) No exemplary damages claimed: the duty's condition is unmet,
-- so this rule asks nothing (case by case, fork F4).
GIVEN `I claim exemplary damages` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`r 8.03(2) -- I must state the exemplary damages claim` `I claim exemplary damages` MEANS
    `yes or no` `I claim exemplary damages`

-- r 8.06: the applicant must "as soon as practicable and at least 5 days before the first directions hearing or the
-- hearing, whichever is the earlier, serve a copy ... personally on each respondent". Five days or less: days that are
-- not business days, and the Christmas break, are not counted (r 1.61(3), (5)).
GIVEN `the first directions hearing` IS A DATE, `the hearing` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`r 8.06 -- the last day to serve the originating application` `the first directions hearing` `the hearing` MEANS
    `r 1.61 -- the last day at least n days before` (`the earlier date of` `the first directions hearing` `the hearing`) 5

§§ `Part 10 -- when a document is served (r 10.32)`

DECLARE `Means of service` IS ONE OF
    `personal service`
    `pre-paid post`
    fax
    `electronic communication`

-- r 10.32: a document served under r 10.31 is taken to be served "(a) if ... sent by pre-paid post--on the seventh
-- business day after the document was sent; (b) ... fax--on the next business day ...; (c) ... electronic
-- communication--on the next business day". Personal service is service on the day the document is handed over
-- (Division 10.1; fork F5).
GIVEN `the day sent` IS A DATE, `the means` IS A `Means of service`
GIVETH A DATE
`r 10.32 -- the day I am taken to be served` `the day sent` `the means` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the means`
    WHEN `personal service` THEN `the day sent`
    WHEN `pre-paid post` THEN `the nth business day after` `the day sent` 7
    WHEN fax THEN `the next business day after` `the day sent`
    WHEN `electronic communication` THEN `the next business day after` `the day sent`

§§ `Division 16.3 -- the defence and reply (rr 16.32, 16.33)`

-- r 16.32: "A respondent must file a defence ... within 28 days after service of the statement of claim."
GIVEN `the day the statement of claim was served` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`r 16.32 -- the last day to file a defence` `the day the statement of claim was served` MEANS
    `the last day to file` `the day the statement of claim was served` 28

-- r 16.33: the applicant who wants to plead a r 16.08 matter "must file a reply ... within 14 days after being served
-- with the defence".
GIVEN `the day the defence was served` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`r 16.33 -- the last day to file a reply` `the day the defence was served` MEANS
    `the last day to file` `the day the defence was served` 14

DECLARE `Pleading party` IS ONE OF `the respondent`
DECLARE `Pleading action` IS ONE OF `file a defence`

-- r 16.32 as a duty, counted in days from service of the statement of claim to the last day.
GIVEN `days allowed` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Pleading party` `Pleading action`
`r 16.32 -- the respondent must file a defence` `days allowed` MEANS
    PARTY `the respondent`
    MUST `file a defence`
    WITHIN `days allowed`
    LEST BREACH BY `the respondent` BECAUSE "no defence within 28 days after service of the statement of claim (r 16.32): the respondent is in default (r 5.22(a))"

-- Runs the duty: was the defence filed in time? Takes plain dates only; not exported.
GIVEN `the day the statement of claim was served` IS A DATE, `the day the defence was filed` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`r 16.32 -- the defence was filed in time` `the day the statement of claim was served` `the day the defence was filed` MEANS
    CONSIDER EVALTRACE (`r 16.32 -- the respondent must file a defence` `days allowed`) 0 `the events`
    WHEN FULFILLED THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE
    WHERE
        `days allowed` MEANS `days from` `the day the statement of claim was served` (`r 16.32 -- the last day to file a defence` `the day the statement of claim was served`)
        `day filed` MEANS `days from` `the day the statement of claim was served` `the day the defence was filed`
        `the events` MEANS
            LIST (EVENT `the respondent` `file a defence` `day filed`), (WAITUNTIL (`day filed` PLUS `days allowed` PLUS 2))

§§ `Division 5.2 -- default (rr 5.22, 5.23)`

-- r 5.22: "A party is in default if the party fails to: (a) do an act required ..., or to do an act in the time
-- required, by these Rules; or (b) comply with an order of the Court; or (c) attend a hearing ...; or (d) prosecute or
-- defend the proceeding with due diligence." Read as the definition of default: none of (a)-(d), no default (fork F6).
-- Here only (a) is worked out, for the defence: no defence by the last day, or a defence filed after it (fork F7: a
-- late defence was still a failure "to do an act in the time required"). The other heads are inputs.
GIVEN `the day the statement of claim was served` IS A DATE, `a defence has been filed` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `the day the defence was filed` IS A DATE, `today` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `rr 5.22(a), 16.32 -- the respondent failed to file a defence in time` `the day the statement of claim was served` `a defence has been filed` `the day the defence was filed` `today` IF
    IF `a defence has been filed` AND `is on or before` `the day the defence was filed` `today`
    THEN NOT (`r 16.32 -- the defence was filed in time` `the day the statement of claim was served` `the day the defence was filed`)
    ELSE NOT (`is on or before` `today` (`r 16.32 -- the last day to file a defence` `the day the statement of claim was served`))

GIVEN `the day the statement of claim was served` IS A DATE, `a defence has been filed` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `the day the defence was filed` IS A DATE, `today` IS A DATE,
      `failed to comply with an order` IS A BOOLEAN, `failed to attend a hearing` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `failed to defend with due diligence` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`r 5.22 -- the respondent is in default` `the day the statement of claim was served` `a defence has been filed` `the day the defence was filed` `today` `failed to comply with an order` `failed to attend a hearing` `failed to defend with due diligence` MEANS
    `yes or no`
        (    `rr 5.22(a), 16.32 -- the respondent failed to file a defence in time` `the day the statement of claim was served` `a defence has been filed` `the day the defence was filed` `today`
         OR `failed to comply with an order`
         OR `failed to attend a hearing`
         OR `failed to defend with due diligence`)

DECLARE `Default order` IS ONE OF
    `no order on default, because the respondent is not in default`
    `judgment for the debt or liquidated damages, with interest and costs if appropriate`
    `judgment for the relief claimed in my statement of claim to which the Court is satisfied I am entitled, or for damages to be assessed`
    `judgment for damages to be assessed, or any other order`

-- r 5.23(2): "If a respondent is in default, an applicant may apply to the Court for: (a) ... a step ...; (b) if the claim
-- ... is for a debt or liquidated damages--... judgment ... for (i) the debt or liquidated damages; and (ii) if
-- appropriate, interest and costs ...; (c) if the proceeding was started by an originating application supported by a
-- statement of claim [or alternative document, or ordered onto pleadings]--... judgment ... for the relief claimed ...
-- to which the Court is satisfied that the applicant is entitled; or (d) ... judgment ... for damages to be assessed, or
-- any other order". The answer names the fullest judgment open; (a) and (d) are always open in default.
GIVEN `the respondent is in default` IS A BOOLEAN, `my claim is for a debt or liquidated damages` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `my claim is on pleadings` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Default order`
`r 5.23(2) -- the judgment I can apply for` `the respondent is in default` `my claim is for a debt or liquidated damages` `my claim is on pleadings` MEANS
    IF NOT `the respondent is in default`
    THEN `no order on default, because the respondent is not in default`
    ELSE IF `my claim is for a debt or liquidated damages`
         THEN `judgment for the debt or liquidated damages, with interest and costs if appropriate`
         ELSE IF `my claim is on pleadings`
              THEN `judgment for the relief claimed in my statement of claim to which the Court is satisfied I am entitled, or for damages to be assessed`
              ELSE `judgment for damages to be assessed, or any other order`

§§ `Division 23.3 -- examinations by a medical expert (r 23.21)`

DECLARE `Examination basis` IS ONE OF
    `a notice from another party requesting it`
    `an order of the Court`
    `neither`

-- r 23.21(1): the rule applies if "(a) a person's ... physical or mental condition is relevant to a matter in question;
-- and (b) the relevant person is a party or a person for whose benefit a party is claiming relief". Outside it, the rule
-- is silent. NOTHING-kind: scope limit.
GIVEN `my condition is in question` IS A BOOLEAN, `I am a party or claimed for` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `r 23.21(1) -- the rule applies to me` `my condition is in question` `I am a party or claimed for` IF
    `my condition is in question` AND `I am a party or claimed for`

-- r 23.21(2), (6), (7): a notice only "request[s]" an examination; an order "require[s]" it, and then the person "must
-- do all things reasonably requested, and answer all questions reasonably asked". On a notice alone the rule states no
-- duty. NOTHING-kind: silent (fork F8: the Court can order it under (6)).
GIVEN `my condition is in question` IS A BOOLEAN, `I am a party or claimed for` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `the basis` IS AN `Examination basis`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`r 23.21 -- I must submit to the examination` `my condition is in question` `I am a party or claimed for` `the basis` MEANS
    IF NOT `r 23.21(1) -- the rule applies to me` `my condition is in question` `I am a party or claimed for`
    THEN NOTHING
    ELSE CONSIDER `the basis`
         WHEN `an order of the Court` THEN JUST TRUE
         OTHERWISE NOTHING

-- r 23.21(3): "The relevant person may have a medical expert of their choice attend the examination." (8): "medical
-- expert means a person who, under a law of a State or Territory, is registered or licenced to practice in a health
-- profession or allied health profession". Someone who is not a medical expert: the rule is silent. NOTHING-kind:
-- grant's wording.
GIVEN `my condition is in question` IS A BOOLEAN, `I am a party or claimed for` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `the basis` IS AN `Examination basis`, `my expert is registered or licensed in a health profession` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`r 23.21(3) -- I may bring my own medical expert` `my condition is in question` `I am a party or claimed for` `the basis` `my expert is registered or licensed in a health profession` MEANS
    IF (NOT (`r 23.21(1) -- the rule applies to me` `my condition is in question` `I am a party or claimed for`)) OR (`the basis` EQUALS `neither`)
    THEN NOTHING
    ELSE IF `my expert is registered or licensed in a health profession`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE NOTHING

-- r 23.21(4): "A party who serves a notice under subrule (2) must, on request by the relevant person, pay ... a
-- reasonable sum to meet the travel and other expenses ..., including the expenses of having a medical expert chosen
-- by the relevant person attend". (5): that party must, "as soon as reasonably practicable after the examination",
-- obtain the expert's report and serve a copy on the relevant person. Both duties are tied to a notice; for an
-- examination on the Court's order alone the rule is silent. NOTHING-kind: silent. Not yet requested: the duty arises
-- "on request" (case by case, fork F9: JUST FALSE until requested).
GIVEN `my condition is in question` IS A BOOLEAN, `I am a party or claimed for` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `the basis` IS AN `Examination basis`, `I asked for my expenses` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`r 23.21(4) -- the other party must pay my expenses` `my condition is in question` `I am a party or claimed for` `the basis` `I asked for my expenses` MEANS
    IF NOT `r 23.21(1) -- the rule applies to me` `my condition is in question` `I am a party or claimed for`
    THEN NOTHING
    ELSE CONSIDER `the basis`
         WHEN `a notice from another party requesting it` THEN `yes or no` `I asked for my expenses`
         OTHERWISE NOTHING

GIVEN `my condition is in question` IS A BOOLEAN, `I am a party or claimed for` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `the basis` IS AN `Examination basis`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`r 23.21(5) -- I must be served with the report` `my condition is in question` `I am a party or claimed for` `the basis` MEANS
    IF NOT `r 23.21(1) -- the rule applies to me` `my condition is in question` `I am a party or claimed for`
    THEN NOTHING
    ELSE CONSIDER `the basis`
         WHEN `a notice from another party requesting it` THEN JUST TRUE
         OTHERWISE NOTHING

§§ `Part 25 -- offers to settle`

-- r 25.05(3) and r 25.08(1): the time for acceptance "must not be less than 14 days after the offer is made". A period
-- fixed by the Rules, so r 1.61(2) and (5) apply (fork F10); acceptance is served, not filed.
GIVEN `the day the offer was made` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`r 25.08(1) -- the earliest closing day an offer may state` `the day the offer was made` MEANS
    `the last day to act` `the day the offer was made` 14

-- "must not be less than": a flat negative, so a shorter time is the text's no.
GIVEN `the day the offer was made` IS A DATE, `the closing day stated` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`r 25.08(1) -- the time for acceptance is long enough` `the day the offer was made` `the closing day stated` MEANS
    `yes or no` (`is on or before` (`r 25.08(1) -- the earliest closing day an offer may state` `the day the offer was made`) `the closing day stated`)

-- r 25.08: (1) "open to be accepted within the time stated in the notice"; (2) "If no time for acceptance is stated ...
-- at any time before judgment is given"; (3) acceptance "at any time while the offer is open". A withdrawn offer
-- (r 25.07) is not open. A stated time shorter than r 25.08(1) allows is read up to the earliest lawful closing day
-- (fork F11). "Within the time stated": a period in the text's words, so after it, no.
GIVEN `the day the offer was made` IS A DATE, `a closing day is stated` IS A BOOLEAN, `the closing day stated` IS A DATE,
      `the offer has been withdrawn` IS A BOOLEAN, `judgment has been given` IS A BOOLEAN, `the day I accept` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`r 25.08 -- I can accept the offer` `the day the offer was made` `a closing day is stated` `the closing day stated` `the offer has been withdrawn` `judgment has been given` `the day I accept` MEANS
    IF `judgment has been given` OR `the offer has been withdrawn` OR (NOT (`is on or before` `the day the offer was made` `the day I accept`))
    THEN JUST FALSE
    ELSE IF `a closing day is stated`
         THEN `yes or no` (`is on or before` `the day I accept` (`the later date of` `the closing day stated` (`r 25.08(1) -- the earliest closing day an offer may state` `the day the offer was made`)))
         ELSE JUST TRUE

-- r 25.07: "An offer may be withdrawn within 14 days after it is made only if: (a) the Court, on an application by the
-- offeror, gives leave; or (b) the offer is superseded by an offer in more favourable terms to the offeree." Within the
-- 14 days: "only if". After them the rule is silent. NOTHING-kind: silent (fork F12; an offer with a stated closing day
-- may still have to stay open till then under r 25.08(1)).
GIVEN `the day the offer was made` IS A DATE, `the day I withdraw` IS A DATE, `the Court gives leave` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `superseded by a more favourable offer` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`r 25.07 -- I can withdraw my offer` `the day the offer was made` `the day I withdraw` `the Court gives leave` `superseded by a more favourable offer` MEANS
    IF `is on or before` `the day I withdraw` (`the last day to act` `the day the offer was made` 14)
    THEN `yes or no` (`the Court gives leave` OR `superseded by a more favourable offer`)
    ELSE NOTHING

-- r 25.04: "An offer to pay a sum of money is, unless the notice provides otherwise, taken to be an offer that the sum
-- will be paid within 28 days after acceptance of the offer." A period fixed by the Rules: r 1.61 applies (fork F10).
GIVEN `the day I accepted` IS A DATE, `the offer states its own time for payment` IS A BOOLEAN, `the payment day stated` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`r 25.04 -- the last day for payment` `the day I accepted` `the offer states its own time for payment` `the payment day stated` MEANS
    IF `the offer states its own time for payment`
    THEN `the payment day stated`
    ELSE `the last day to act` `the day I accepted` 28

DECLARE `Offer party` IS ONE OF `the offeror`
DECLARE `Offer action` IS ONE OF `pay the sum offered`

-- r 25.04 as a duty of the offeror, counted in days from acceptance.
GIVEN `days allowed` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Offer party` `Offer action`
`r 25.04 -- the offeror must pay` `days allowed` MEANS
    PARTY `the offeror`
    MUST `pay the sum offered`
    WITHIN `days allowed`
    LEST BREACH BY `the offeror` BECAUSE "sum not paid within the time for payment (r 25.04): the offeree may seek leave to withdraw the acceptance (r 25.09) or apply under r 25.10"

-- Runs the duty: was the sum paid in time? Takes plain dates only; not exported.
GIVEN `the day I accepted` IS A DATE, `the last day for payment` IS A DATE, `the day paid` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`r 25.04 -- the sum was paid in time` `the day I accepted` `the last day for payment` `the day paid` MEANS
    CONSIDER EVALTRACE (`r 25.04 -- the offeror must pay` `days allowed`) 0 `the events`
    WHEN FULFILLED THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE
    WHERE
        `days allowed` MEANS `days from` `the day I accepted` `the last day for payment`
        `day paid` MEANS `days from` `the day I accepted` `the day paid`
        `the events` MEANS
            LIST (EVENT `the offeror` `pay the sum offered` `day paid`), (WAITUNTIL (`day paid` PLUS `days allowed` PLUS 2))

-- r 25.09(1): "An offeree who has accepted an offer for a sum of money may withdraw the acceptance if: (a) the sum of
-- money is not paid within 28 days after acceptance ... or within the time provided by the offer; and (b) the Court, on
-- the application of the party who accepted the offer, gives leave." An "if": either unmet, no. Not yet paid but the
-- time still running: (a) is not yet met.
GIVEN `the day I accepted` IS A DATE, `the offer states its own time for payment` IS A BOOLEAN, `the payment day stated` IS A DATE,
      `the sum has been paid` IS A BOOLEAN, `the day paid` IS A DATE, `today` IS A DATE, `the Court gives leave` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`r 25.09 -- I can withdraw my acceptance` `the day I accepted` `the offer states its own time for payment` `the payment day stated` `the sum has been paid` `the day paid` `today` `the Court gives leave` MEANS
    `yes or no` (`not paid in time` AND `the Court gives leave`)
    WHERE
        `the last day` MEANS `r 25.04 -- the last day for payment` `the day I accepted` `the offer states its own time for payment` `the payment day stated`
        `not paid in time` MEANS
            IF `the sum has been paid` AND `is on or before` `the day paid` `today`
            THEN NOT (`r 25.04 -- the sum was paid in time` `the day I accepted` `the last day` `the day paid`)
            ELSE NOT (`is on or before` `today` `the last day`)

-- r 25.12: "If an offer does not include the offeree's costs of the proceeding and the offeree accepts the offer, the
-- offeree may tax costs on a party and party basis against the offeror up to and including 14 days after the offer was
-- made." Not a time for doing an act, so counted in plain days, the day of the offer not counted (fork F13).
GIVEN `the day the offer was made` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`r 25.12 -- my costs run up to` `the day the offer was made` MEANS
    `the day n days after` `the day the offer was made` 14

-- r 25.13(2), r 25.14: "11.00 am on the second business day after the offer was served". Business days in the rule's own
-- words; r 1.61(5) is not applied, since this is not a time for doing an act (fork F13).
GIVEN `the day the offer was served` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`r 25.14 -- the day of the 11 am cut-off` `the day the offer was served` MEANS
    `the nth business day after` `the day the offer was served` 2

DECLARE `Who made the offer` IS ONE OF
    `the respondent made the offer to me`
    `I made the offer to the respondent`

DECLARE `How my claim ended` IS ONE OF
    `I got judgment less favourable to me than the offer`
    `I got judgment as favourable to me as the offer`
    `I got judgment more favourable to me than the offer`
    `my proceeding was dismissed`

DECLARE `Offer costs consequence` IS ONE OF
    `rule 25.14 does not apply`
    `I get no costs after the cut-off and must pay the respondent's costs after it on an indemnity basis`
    `I must pay the respondent's costs, on a party and party basis before the cut-off and an indemnity basis after it`
    `the respondent must pay my costs, on a party and party basis before the cut-off and an indemnity basis after it`

-- r 25.14, from the applicant's seat. (1) respondent's offer not accepted, judgment "less favourable than the terms of
-- the offer"; (2) respondent's offer, the applicant "unreasonably fails to accept" and the proceeding "is dismissed";
-- (3) applicant's offer not accepted, judgment "more favourable than the terms of the offer". Each an "if"; outside
-- all three the rule gives no consequence and costs follow the ordinary rules. A judgment exactly as favourable as the
-- offer is in none of them (finding 3). Whether the failure was unreasonable is the Court's judgment, an input.
GIVEN `who made it` IS A `Who made the offer`, `the offer was accepted` IS A BOOLEAN, `the outcome` IS A `How my claim ended`,
      `the Court finds I unreasonably failed to accept` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH AN `Offer costs consequence`
`r 25.14 -- the costs consequence of the offer` `who made it` `the offer was accepted` `the outcome` `the Court finds I unreasonably failed to accept` MEANS
    IF `the offer was accepted`
    THEN `rule 25.14 does not apply`
    ELSE CONSIDER `who made it`
         WHEN `the respondent made the offer to me` THEN
             CONSIDER `the outcome`
             WHEN `I got judgment less favourable to me than the offer` THEN `I get no costs after the cut-off and must pay the respondent's costs after it on an indemnity basis`
             WHEN `my proceeding was dismissed` THEN
                 IF `the Court finds I unreasonably failed to accept`
                 THEN `I must pay the respondent's costs, on a party and party basis before the cut-off and an indemnity basis after it`
                 ELSE `rule 25.14 does not apply`
             OTHERWISE `rule 25.14 does not apply`
         WHEN `I made the offer to the respondent` THEN
             CONSIDER `the outcome`
             WHEN `I got judgment more favourable to me than the offer` THEN `the respondent must pay my costs, on a party and party basis before the cut-off and an indemnity basis after it`
             OTHERWISE `rule 25.14 does not apply`

§§ `Part 26 -- summary judgment and discontinuance`

-- r 26.01(3): a summary judgment application and affidavit "must be served on the party against whom the order is
-- sought at least 14 days before the hearing of the application". Over 5 days: weekends count; the Christmas break does
-- not (r 1.61(5)).
GIVEN `the hearing of the application` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`r 26.01(3) -- the last day to serve a summary judgment application` `the hearing of the application` MEANS
    `r 1.61 -- the last day at least n days before` `the hearing of the application` 14

DECLARE `Way to discontinue` IS ONE OF
    `without the Court's leave or the other party's consent`
    `with the other party's consent or the Court's leave`
    `only with the Court's leave`

-- r 26.12(2): (a) without leave or consent "(i) at any time before the earlier of the first directions hearing and the
-- hearing; or (ii) if the proceeding is continuing on pleadings--at any time before the pleadings have closed"; (b) with
-- consent "before judgment has been entered"; (c) with leave "at any time". (4): "a litigation representative or a
-- representative party must not discontinue a party's claim without first obtaining the leave of the Court".
GIVEN `the first directions hearing` IS A DATE, `the hearing` IS A DATE, `the day I discontinue` IS A DATE,
      `the proceeding is on pleadings` IS A BOOLEAN, `the pleadings have closed` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `judgment has been entered` IS A BOOLEAN, `I act as litigation representative or representative party` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Way to discontinue`
`r 26.12 -- how I can discontinue` `the first directions hearing` `the hearing` `the day I discontinue` `the proceeding is on pleadings` `the pleadings have closed` `judgment has been entered` `I act as litigation representative or representative party` MEANS
    IF `I act as litigation representative or representative party`
    THEN `only with the Court's leave`
    ELSE IF    (NOT (`is on or before` (`the earlier date of` `the first directions hearing` `the hearing`) `the day I discontinue`))
            OR (`the proceeding is on pleadings` AND (NOT `the pleadings have closed`))
         THEN `without the Court's leave or the other party's consent`
         ELSE IF NOT `judgment has been entered`
              THEN `with the other party's consent or the Court's leave`
              ELSE `only with the Court's leave`

-- r 26.12(7): "Unless the terms of a consent or an order of the Court provide otherwise, a party who files a notice of
-- discontinuance under subrule (2) is liable to pay the costs of each other party ... in relation to the claim, or part
-- of the claim, that is discontinued." "Unless": when the terms provide otherwise, the text's no.
GIVEN `a consent or order provides otherwise` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`r 26.12(7) -- I must pay the other side's costs of what I discontinue` `a consent or order provides otherwise` MEANS
    `yes or no` (NOT `a consent or order provides otherwise`)

DECLARE `How my earlier proceeding ended` IS ONE OF
    `I discontinued it and became liable for the other party's costs`
    `it was dismissed and I was ordered to pay the other party's costs`
    `some other way`

-- r 26.15 and r 39.03(2): the opposing party "may apply ... for an order that a subsequent proceeding be stayed until
-- the costs are paid" if the earlier proceeding was discontinued with a costs liability (r 26.15) or dismissed with a
-- costs order (r 39.03(2)), and the new proceeding is on the same or substantially the same cause of action. r 26.14:
-- the discontinuance itself "cannot be pleaded as a defence" to the new proceeding. Each an "if": unmet, no.
GIVEN `how it ended` IS A `How my earlier proceeding ended`, `I have paid those costs` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `the new claim is on the same or substantially the same cause` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`rr 26.15, 39.03(2) -- my new proceeding can be stayed until I pay` `how it ended` `I have paid those costs` `the new claim is on the same or substantially the same cause` MEANS
    CONSIDER `how it ended`
    WHEN `some other way` THEN JUST FALSE
    OTHERWISE `yes or no` ((NOT `I have paid those costs`) AND `the new claim is on the same or substantially the same cause`)

§§ `Division 30.4 -- damages calculated by a Registrar (rr 30.41-30.43)`

-- r 30.41(1): an applicant may apply for an order that damages be calculated by a Registrar "if: (a) a respondent
-- admits liability ... but denies liability to the extent of the damages claimed; or (b) the Court finds that a party is
-- liable to pay damages". The Note: the Court makes the order if satisfied that the amount is "substantially a matter of
-- calculation" (an input).
GIVEN `liability admitted but not the amount` IS A BOOLEAN, `the Court found liability for damages` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `the Court is satisfied it is substantially calculation` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`r 30.41 -- my damages can be calculated by a Registrar` `liability admitted but not the amount` `the Court found liability for damages` `the Court is satisfied it is substantially calculation` MEANS
    `yes or no` ((`liability admitted but not the amount` OR `the Court found liability for damages`) AND `the Court is satisfied it is substantially calculation`)

-- r 30.42: object "within 7 days after receiving the Registrar's certificate": give the Registrar notice and serve each
-- other party. Seven days: over 5, so weekends count; the Christmas break does not. Giving a notice to the Registrar is
-- lodging with the Registry, done on business days (r 1.61(4); fork F3).
GIVEN `the day I received the certificate` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`r 30.42 -- the last day to object to the certificate` `the day I received the certificate` MEANS
    `the last day to file` `the day I received the certificate` 7

-- r 30.43: the objector "must, within 21 days after giving notice, apply to the Court for an order that the Court assess
-- the amount of damages payable".
GIVEN `the day I gave notice` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`r 30.43 -- the last day to apply for the Court to assess damages` `the day I gave notice` MEANS
    `the last day to file` `the day I gave notice` 21

§§ `Parts 35 and 36 -- leave to appeal and appeals`

-- r 35.13: the application for leave "must be filed: (a) within 14 days after the date on which the judgment was
-- pronounced or the order was made; or (b) on or before a date fixed for that purpose by the Court". Either is enough,
-- so the later of the two (fork F14).
GIVEN `the day of the judgment` IS A DATE, `the Court fixed a date` IS A BOOLEAN, `the date fixed` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`r 35.13 -- the last day to apply for leave to appeal` `the day of the judgment` `the Court fixed a date` `the date fixed` MEANS
    IF `the Court fixed a date`
    THEN `the later date of` `the date fixed` (`the last day to file` `the day of the judgment` 14)
    ELSE `the last day to file` `the day of the judgment` 14

-- r 35.15: serve the application and documents "within 2 days of filing". Two days: only business days count.
GIVEN `the day I filed` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`r 35.15 -- the last day to serve the leave application` `the day I filed` MEANS
    `the last day to act` `the day I filed` 2

DECLARE `Kind of appeal` IS ONE OF
    `an appeal as of right`
    `an appeal by leave`

-- r 36.03: "within 28 days after: (i) the date on which the judgment appealed from was pronounced or the order was
-- made; or (ii) the date on which leave to appeal was granted; or (b) on or before a date fixed for that purpose by the
-- court appealed from". For an appeal by leave, the 28 days run from the grant of leave (fork F15); a date fixed, if
-- later, is enough.
GIVEN `the kind` IS A `Kind of appeal`, `the day of the judgment` IS A DATE, `the day leave was granted` IS A DATE,
      `the court fixed a date` IS A BOOLEAN, `the date fixed` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`r 36.03 -- the last day to file a notice of appeal` `the kind` `the day of the judgment` `the day leave was granted` `the court fixed a date` `the date fixed` MEANS
    IF `the court fixed a date`
    THEN `the later date of` `the date fixed` (`the last day to file` `the start` 28)
    ELSE `the last day to file` `the start` 28
    WHERE
        `the start` MEANS
            CONSIDER `the kind`
            WHEN `an appeal by leave` THEN `the day leave was granted`
            WHEN `an appeal as of right` THEN `the day of the judgment`

-- r 36.04(2): if the court appealed from is a State or Territory court, lodge a copy of the notice of appeal with it
-- "within 7 days after filing the notice of appeal".
GIVEN `the day I filed` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`r 36.04(2) -- the last day to lodge a copy with the State or Territory court` `the day I filed` MEANS
    `the last day to file` `the day I filed` 7

-- r 36.10: "An appellant may, without the Court's leave, amend a notice of appeal during the period of 28 days after
-- filing the notice of appeal". A period in the text's own words: outside it, no (for amendment without leave).
GIVEN `the day I filed` IS A DATE, `the day I amend` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`r 36.10 -- I can amend my notice of appeal without leave` `the day I filed` `the day I amend` MEANS
    `yes or no` (`is on or before` `the day I amend` (`the last day to file` `the day I filed` 28))

DECLARE `Respondent's appeal step` IS ONE OF
    `a notice of address for service`
    `a notice of cross-appeal`
    `a notice of contention`

-- r 36.07: a respondent to an appeal "must file a notice of address for service within 14 days after being served".
-- r 36.22: a cross-appeal "within 21 days after being served with a notice of appeal". r 36.24: a notice of contention
-- "within 21 days after the notice of appeal is served".
GIVEN `the step` IS A `Respondent's appeal step`, `the day I was served with the notice of appeal` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`rr 36.07, 36.22, 36.24 -- the last day for my step in the appeal` `the step` `the day I was served with the notice of appeal` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the step`
    WHEN `a notice of address for service` THEN `the last day to file` `the day I was served with the notice of appeal` 14
    WHEN `a notice of cross-appeal` THEN `the last day to file` `the day I was served with the notice of appeal` 21
    WHEN `a notice of contention` THEN `the last day to file` `the day I was served with the notice of appeal` 21

§§ `Part 39 -- orders, setting aside, interest on judgments`

-- r 39.02: "A person ordered to do an act or thing or to pay money into Court must do so in the time specified in the
-- order or, if no time is specified, within 14 days after the date of service of the order on the person." Not every
-- act ordered is a business-day act, so r 1.61(4) is not applied (fork F16).
GIVEN `the order specifies a time` IS A BOOLEAN, `the last day specified` IS A DATE, `the day the order was served on me` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`r 39.02 -- the last day to comply with the order` `the order specifies a time` `the last day specified` `the day the order was served on me` MEANS
    IF `the order specifies a time`
    THEN `the last day specified`
    ELSE `the last day to act` `the day the order was served on me` 14

DECLARE `Ground to set aside after entry` IS ONE OF
    `it was made in my absence`
    `it was obtained by fraud`
    `it is interlocutory`
    `it is an injunction or appoints a receiver`
    `it does not reflect the intention of the Court`
    `the party it favours consents`
    `there is a clerical mistake in it`
    `there is an error from an accidental slip or omission`
    `none of these`

-- r 39.04(1): before entry the Court "may vary or set aside a judgment or order". (2): an application "filed within 14
-- days after the judgment or order is entered" is dealt with "as if the judgment or order had not been entered"; (4) the
-- Court may not extend that time. r 39.05: after entry, "if" one of grounds (a)-(h). An "if": no ground and out of time,
-- no under these rules (fork F17: r 39.04(5) keeps any other power).
GIVEN `the judgment has been entered` IS A BOOLEAN, `the day it was entered` IS A DATE, `the day I apply` IS A DATE,
      `the ground` IS A `Ground to set aside after entry`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`rr 39.04, 39.05 -- the judgment can be set aside or varied` `the judgment has been entered` `the day it was entered` `the day I apply` `the ground` MEANS
    IF NOT `the judgment has been entered`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE IF `is on or before` `the day I apply` (`the last day to file` `the day it was entered` 14)
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE `yes or no` (NOT (`the ground` EQUALS `none of these`))

-- r 39.06: the prescribed rate of interest on a judgment debt (s 52(2)(a) of the Act) for each half-year (1 January to
-- 30 June, 1 July to 31 December) is "6% above the cash rate last published by the Reserve Bank of Australia before the
-- period commenced". Rates in percentage points. s 52(2)(b) of the Act lets the Court set a lower rate where justice
-- requires; not computed.
GIVEN `the cash rate before the half-year began` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`r 39.06 -- the interest rate on a judgment debt` `the cash rate before the half-year began` MEANS
    `the cash rate before the half-year began` PLUS 6

-- The first day of the half-year a day falls in: the cash rate to use is the one last published before it.
GIVEN x IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`r 39.06 -- the start of the half-year` x MEANS
    IF DATE_MONTH x AT MOST 6
    THEN `the day` 1 1 (DATE_YEAR x)
    ELSE `the day` 1 7 (DATE_YEAR x)

§§ `Part 40 -- costs`

DECLARE `Interlocutory costs outcome` IS ONE OF
    `the order on the application was in my favour`
    `the order on the application was in the other party's favour`
    `no order was made in favour of any party`

DECLARE `Interlocutory costs result` IS ONE OF
    `the costs follow the event: the party the order favours gets them`
    `they are costs in the cause of whoever succeeds in the proceeding`
    `the Court's costs order governs`

-- r 40.04: "If no order for costs is made on an interlocutory application or hearing, the costs ...: (a) if an order is
-- made in favour of any party--follow the event; or (b) if no order is made in favour of any party--are taken to be
-- costs in the cause of the successful party to the proceeding."
GIVEN `the Court made a costs order` IS A BOOLEAN, `the outcome` IS AN `Interlocutory costs outcome`
GIVETH AN `Interlocutory costs result`
`r 40.04 -- who bears the interlocutory costs` `the Court made a costs order` `the outcome` MEANS
    IF `the Court made a costs order`
    THEN `the Court's costs order governs`
    ELSE CONSIDER `the outcome`
         WHEN `no order was made in favour of any party` THEN `they are costs in the cause of whoever succeeds in the proceeding`
         OTHERWISE `the costs follow the event: the party the order favours gets them`

-- r 40.08: a party (outside Admiralty proceedings) may apply for an order reducing the costs payable to another party
-- "if: (a) the applicant has claimed a money sum or damages and has been awarded a sum of less than $100 000; or (b) the
-- proceeding ... could more suitably have been brought in another court or tribunal". From the applicant's seat: can my
-- costs be cut? "Less than": $100 000 exactly is not under. (b) is the Court's view, an input. "Other than in a
-- proceeding under the Admiralty Act 1988": read as the text's no (case by case, fork F18).
GIVEN `I claimed money or damages` IS A BOOLEAN, `the sum I was awarded` IS A NUMBER,
      `the Court thinks another court or tribunal was more suitable` IS A BOOLEAN, `it is an Admiralty proceeding` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`r 40.08 -- the costs payable to me can be reduced` `I claimed money or damages` `the sum I was awarded` `the Court thinks another court or tribunal was more suitable` `it is an Admiralty proceeding` MEANS
    IF `it is an Admiralty proceeding`
    THEN JUST FALSE
    ELSE `yes or no` ((`I claimed money or damages` AND `the sum I was awarded` LESS THAN 100000) OR `the Court thinks another court or tribunal was more suitable`)

-- r 40.13: interlocutory costs: the party "must not tax those costs until the proceeding in which the order is made is
-- finished" (the Note: the Court may order immediate taxation). "Until": before it, no.
GIVEN `the proceeding is finished` IS A BOOLEAN, `the Court ordered immediate taxation` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`r 40.13 -- I can tax my interlocutory costs now` `the proceeding is finished` `the Court ordered immediate taxation` MEANS
    `yes or no` (`the proceeding is finished` OR `the Court ordered immediate taxation`)

-- r 40.21(1): to object to the estimate, "within 21 days after the issue of the notice of estimate: (a) file a notice of
-- objection ...; and (b) pay into the Litigants' Fund an amount of $2 000 as security".
GIVEN `the day the notice of estimate issued` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`r 40.21 -- the last day to object to the estimate` `the day the notice of estimate issued` MEANS
    `the last day to file` `the day the notice of estimate issued` 21

`r 40.21(1)(b) -- the security to pay in on objecting` MEANS 2000

-- r 40.23(4): after a provisional taxation, "within 21 days after the date of the written notice", file a notice
-- requesting a full taxation.
GIVEN `the day of the notice` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`r 40.23(4) -- the last day to ask for a full taxation` `the day of the notice` MEANS
    `the last day to file` `the day of the notice` 21

-- r 40.33(1): "A party who files an objection under rule 40.21 must pay the costs of taxation of all parties from the
-- date on which the taxing officer notified the parties of the estimate unless: (a) if the party is the party who filed
-- the bill--the costs are taxed at more than 115% of the taxing officer's estimate; or (b) in any other case--the costs
-- are taxed at less than 85% of the taxing officer's estimate." "Unless": met, no. A party who did not object: the rule
-- is silent. NOTHING-kind: scope limit. (2) lets the objector ask to be relieved; not computed.
GIVEN `I objected to the estimate` IS A BOOLEAN, `I filed the bill` IS A BOOLEAN, `the estimate` IS A NUMBER,
      `the amount taxed` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`r 40.33 -- I must pay the costs of the taxation` `I objected to the estimate` `I filed the bill` `the estimate` `the amount taxed` MEANS
    IF NOT `I objected to the estimate`
    THEN NOTHING
    ELSE IF `I filed the bill`
         THEN `yes or no` (NOT (`the amount taxed` TIMES 100 GREATER THAN `the estimate` TIMES 115))
         ELSE `yes or no` (NOT (`the amount taxed` TIMES 100 LESS THAN `the estimate` TIMES 85))

-- r 40.32(1): the certificate of taxation "must be served, within 14 days after the date it is issued, by the party who
-- filed the bill". r 40.34(4): an application for review "must be filed and served ... within 28 days after the issue of
-- the certificate of taxation".
GIVEN `the day the certificate issued` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`r 40.32 -- the last day to serve the certificate of taxation` `the day the certificate issued` MEANS
    `the last day to act` `the day the certificate issued` 14

GIVEN `the day the certificate issued` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`r 40.34 -- the last day to apply for review of the taxation` `the day the certificate issued` MEANS
    `the last day to file` `the day the certificate issued` 28
